  "query": "How would you design a highly available, horizontally scalable chat application capable of supporting millions of concurrent users with the following requirements:\n        •        Message Delivery Guarantees: Exactly-once delivery.\n        •        Features: Typing indicators, message history, and media sharing.\n        •        Conversation Types: Support for both one-to-one and group chats.\n        •        Security: End-to-end encryption as a desirable feature.\n\nIn your design, compare database selection options (e.g., relational, NoSQL, distributed databases) and justify trade-offs in terms of scalability, latency, and consistency.\n\nThe solution should outline:\n        •        Core Architecture Components (messaging layer, storage layer, real-time event handling).\n        •        Scalability Mechanisms (sharding, partitioning, load balancing).\n        •        High Availability & Fault Tolerance strategies.\n        •        Security & Encryption design for protecting messages in transit and at rest.\n\nNo specific technology stack is required, but nice to have references to proven tools or services (e.g., Kafka, Redis, Cassandra, DynamoDB) for illustrative purposes\n\nTarget audience: Junior developers seeking introductory material"
